# Suite bench (plans 08-18 and 08-19, D-21 to D-26, D-39): tests/bench-tap.sh runs the benchmark tool ivs-bench of each preset in its
# --verify-only mode (no clock is read) against data/bench/workloads.tsv, the scenarios, the goldens and the build-tree images.
# bench.verify.<workload>: the verification run of the workload matches its committed golden and the row says status verified, with
#   empty throughput and latency columns (plan 08-18: bench-lamp-idle, bench-lamp-input, bench-lamp-cold; plan 08-19: bench-lamp-snapshot,
#   the idle scenario run with a save, reset and restore every 30 frames, verified against the idle golden, its static counts equal to
#   those of the idle row, and a run in which the round-trip hook made no cut is a harness failure of the tool).
bench.verify.bench-lamp-idle
bench.verify.bench-lamp-input
bench.verify.bench-lamp-cold
bench.verify.bench-lamp-snapshot
# bench.mutant.refuse-mutated-golden (D-22, D-25): a golden with one digest line changed is refused: exit 15, the bench-refuse line, a
#   refused row with no measurement, in a verify-only run and in a run of one timed iteration.
# bench.refuse.wrong-ticks: a workload table whose ticks differ from the golden is refused the same way.
# bench.refuse.bad-args: usage and harness errors end with exit 14, one stderr line and no row.
# bench.tsv.format: the format line, the header, the three groups, the field count, the tier and ci_time text.
# bench.judge.refuse-has-no-timing: the absence-of-measurement checker rejects a synthetic refused row that carries a value.
bench.mutant.refuse-mutated-golden
bench.refuse.wrong-ticks
bench.refuse.bad-args
bench.tsv.format
bench.judge.refuse-has-no-timing
# bench.workloads.table-consistent (plan 08-19, D-23): the workload table is consistent with the scenario inventory, the scenario files
#   and the goldens (files and text only, nothing is run); three scratch tables broken one way each show that the rules can fail.
bench.workloads.table-consistent
# bench.baseline.record-format (plan 08-19, D-24, T-08-43): every committed data/bench/baseline-*.tsv has the format line, the exact
#   header, the three provenance comment lines, one measured row per workload of the table in order (optimized 1, sanitizers off, the
#   table counts, positive figures, the ci_time pointer); four broken scratch records show the rules can fail; no number is compared.
bench.baseline.record-format
